.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# data/ IS committed: the vector index is built on the GPU machine and shipped
# through git, because the host has no GPU and the two are on different networks.
# One machine builds; everyone else pulls and serves. Consequences:
#   - storage.sqlite is ~31 MB of binary, and a fresh copy enters history on
#     every rebuild. History cannot be pruned without rewriting it.
#   - it cannot merge. If two machines both build, one side's work is discarded.
#   - stop the server before pulling: the embedded store is a locked file, and a
#     running server holds the old one open.

# secrets: QDRANT_API_KEY, MCP_TEAM_PASSWORD, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
.env

# extracted/ IS committed: it is the cached PDF text every later stage was tuned
# against, and one book's copy is OCR output that cannot be regenerated from its
# scanned PDF.

# Runtime noise, not data -- keep it out even when data/ is committed.
data/serve.log
*.log
data/qdrant/*.lock
